+# MapViewer3D Live Data
+
+**Status:** Optional | **Last Updated:** October 2026
+
+The Live Map reads Postgres, so it shows players, vehicles and bases but not
+sandworms, NPCs or sandstorms: those exist only in the memory of the running
+game server processes. The optional `mapviewer-live` stack
+([MapViewer3D, branch `ddp`](https://github.com/dev-prophet-code/MapViewer3D/tree/ddp))
+reads them there, read-only, and streams them to a MapViewer3D running on an
+administrator's PC.
+
+It runs next to the Console as its own compose project and changes nothing in
+the Dune containers:
+
+- `mvagent` – reads `/proc/<pid>/mem` of the game servers (`pid: host`,
+  `SYS_PTRACE` + `DAC_OVERRIDE` only, read-only file system, internal network,
+  no published port, no internet).
+- `mvgate` – the only published port (8797/TCP). TLS 1.3 only, its own key
+  pinned by the viewer, and a mutual token proof bound to the TLS session; the
+  token never crosses the network. Non-root.
+
+## Settings → MapViewer3D Live Data
+
+| Element | What it does |
+|---|---|
+| Status | `Not Installed`, `Stopped`, `Starting`, `Running` or `Unhealthy`, from the `mvgate` container (compose labels `mapviewer-live` / `mvgate`), plus the key fingerprint (`sha256/…`, not secret). |
+| Public Address | Host name or IP the viewers use; port 8797 is added unless `host:port` is given. Validated before it reaches Docker. |
+| Create Pairing Code | Runs `mvgate -pair <address>` in the container and shows the code **once** (copy button, "I've Saved It" removes it). It is not stored, cached or written to the audit log; the audit row records only address and fingerprint. Over plain HTTP the Console warns first, because the code would cross the network unencrypted. |
+| Revoke All Pairings | Runs `mvgate -rotate-token` and restarts `mvgate`; every pairing code stops working. Asks for confirmation. |
+
+When the stack is not installed the section shows the three install commands
+instead of the pairing controls.
+
+## API
+
+| Route | Action | Notes |
+|---|---|---|
+| `GET /api/settings/mapviewer-live` | `settings:read` | status, health, fingerprint – no secret |
+| `POST /api/settings/mapviewer-live/pairing-code` | `settings:write` | body `{ "publicAddress": "…" }` → `{ code, address, fingerprint }`, `cache-control: no-store` |
+| `POST /api/settings/mapviewer-live/revoke` | `settings:write` | rotate token + restart |
+| `GET /api/mapviewer-live/status` | `maps:read` | `{ "available": true\|false, "version": 1 }` for MapViewer3D; no address, pin or token; cached 15 s |
+
+API keys can never hold `settings:*`, so a pairing code can only be created by
+a signed-in administrator. MapViewer3D (Beta.16 or newer) asks the status
+route with its read-only API key; without an answer it hides its live layers.
+An `available: true` answer alone unlocks nothing – the viewer still needs a
+pairing code.
+
+All Docker calls use `execFile` with fixed arguments (`services/mapViewerLive.js`).
+
+Security model and protocol: [MapViewer3D SECURITY.md](https://github.com/dev-prophet-code/MapViewer3D/blob/ddp/SECURITY.md).
